        <mxCell id="D0tRHAQ9LQ57oHEz4JKX-37" value="&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 24px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Knowledge: Learning that a statement is valid or sound&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=default;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1910" y="-200" width="760" height="590" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="D0tRHAQ9LQ57oHEz4JKX-38" value="&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 18px;&quot;&gt;$$\begin{gathered}&lt;br&gt;\boldsymbol{M} \;=\; \frac{A_{n+1}}{A_n} \;=\;&lt;br&gt;\frac{3^{n+1}\sum_{p=1}^{n}&lt;br&gt;\binom{n+1}{p}\; 3^{\;p(n-p+1)}}&lt;br&gt;{3^n\;\sum_{p=1}^{n-1}&lt;br&gt;\binom{n}{p}\; 3^{\,p(n-p)}}&amp;nbsp;\;=\;&lt;br&gt;3\frac{\sum_{p=1}^{n}&lt;br&gt;\binom{n+1}{p}\; 3^{\;p(n+1-p)}}&lt;br&gt;{\sum_{p=1}^{n-1}&lt;br&gt;\binom{n}{p}\; 3^{\,p(n-p)}}&lt;br&gt;\end{gathered}$$&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;spacingTop=0;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1930" y="-30" width="720" height="80" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="D0tRHAQ9LQ57oHEz4JKX-39" value="&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 18px;&quot;&gt;It&#39;s more intuitive to consider the worst-case scenario.&amp;nbsp;The new statement &lt;i&gt;C&lt;/i&gt; adds 3 new possibilities to each of the n statements: {&lt;i&gt;?&lt;/i&gt;, &lt;i&gt;T&lt;/i&gt;, &lt;i&gt;F&lt;/i&gt;} (note: this corresponds to the &lt;i&gt;3&lt;/i&gt;&amp;nbsp;coefficient in &lt;i&gt;M&lt;/i&gt; above). For each of the already existing &lt;i&gt;n&lt;/i&gt;&amp;nbsp;statements, C can connect with all of them 3 different ways: {&lt;i&gt;P&lt;/i&gt;, &lt;i&gt;C&lt;/i&gt;, &lt;i&gt;I&lt;/i&gt;} - which is&amp;nbsp;&lt;i&gt;3&lt;sup&gt;n&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;/i&gt;. Adjusting&amp;nbsp;&lt;i&gt;A&lt;sub&gt;n&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;/i&gt; by these coefficeints leads to &lt;i&gt;M&lt;/i&gt;:&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=0;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;spacingTop=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1920" y="50" width="740" height="100" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="D0tRHAQ9LQ57oHEz4JKX-40" value="&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 18px;&quot;&gt;A statement &lt;i&gt;S&amp;nbsp;&lt;/i&gt;becomes sound when arranging it within &lt;i&gt;k&lt;/i&gt;&amp;nbsp;known&amp;nbsp;statements (ignoring all unknown statements) leaves no contradictions (ie. no two known statements that are both &quot;true&quot; have the &quot;contradicts&quot; relationship). In this case, the only arrangements left will have each &lt;i&gt;k&lt;/i&gt;&amp;nbsp;statement be &quot;true&quot; or &quot;false&quot;, with the rest of the&amp;nbsp;&lt;i&gt;n - k&lt;/i&gt;&amp;nbsp;statements to have all three truth-values.&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=0;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;spacingTop=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1920" y="-150" width="740" height="90" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="D0tRHAQ9LQ57oHEz4JKX-41" value="&lt;span style=&quot;text-wrap-mode: nowrap;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 18px;&quot;&gt;$$\begin{gathered}&lt;br&gt;\boldsymbol{A_{n+1}} \;=\; A_n*3*3^n \;=\; 3^{n+1}A_n&lt;br&gt;\end{gathered}$$&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;spacingTop=0;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1980" y="150" width="340" height="60" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="D0tRHAQ9LQ57oHEz4JKX-42" value="&lt;span style=&quot;text-wrap-mode: nowrap;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 18px;&quot;&gt;$$\begin{gathered}&lt;br&gt;\boldsymbol{M} \;=\; 3^{n+1}\&lt;br&gt;\end{gathered}$$&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;spacingTop=0;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="2340" y="150" width="190" height="60" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="D0tRHAQ9LQ57oHEz4JKX-43" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 18px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Adding a new statement increases the number of arrangements by a maximum of 3&lt;sup&gt;n+1&lt;/sup&gt;, or &lt;i&gt;n+1&lt;/i&gt;&amp;nbsp;in log-space.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;" style="rounded=0;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;spacingTop=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1910" y="320" width="760" height="60" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="D0tRHAQ9LQ57oHEz4JKX-44" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 18px;&quot;&gt;To make the ratio more intuitive (ie. removing the exponent), we can transform it onto the logarithmic scale:&lt;/span&gt;" style="rounded=0;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;spacingTop=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1920" y="220" width="740" height="40" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="D0tRHAQ9LQ57oHEz4JKX-45" value="&lt;span style=&quot;text-wrap-mode: nowrap;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 18px;&quot;&gt;$$\begin{gathered}&lt;br&gt;\boldsymbol{R} \;=\; log_3(M) \;=\; log_3(3^{n+1}) \;=\; n+1&lt;br&gt;\end{gathered}$$&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;spacingTop=0;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="2100" y="260" width="390" height="60" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
